QR/NQR MINIMUM BALANCE  (the base-side meaning of the Paley condition)
  For a QR-supported deck the multiplier orbit collapses to TWO configs (a in QR fixes QR,
  a in NQR swaps to NQR). So M restricted to denominator q = max(min|QR|, min|NQR|)/q.

   q | q%4 | min|c| over QR | over NQR | equal? | Paley section exists?
    7 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   11 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   13 |  1  |        1        |     2    | False  | False
   17 |  1  |        1        |     3    | False  | False
   19 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   23 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   29 |  1  |        1        |     2    | False  | False
   31 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   37 |  1  |        1        |     2    | False  | False
   43 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True
   47 |  3  |        1        |     1    | True   | True

  => the two minima coincide EXACTLY when q = 3 mod 4 = exactly when Paley is a SECTION.
     Reason: q=3 mod 4 => -1 is NQR => -QR = NQR, and |c|_q is +-invariant, so the two
     multisets of absolute residues are IDENTICAL. The section-existence condition has a
     purely base-side meaning: QR/NQR absolute-residue BALANCE.
